To calculate the OpenSSL session keys:

#generate the raw 256-bit private key
openssl genkey -algorithm x25519 -out browser_private_key.pem
openssl genkey -algorithm x25519 -out server_private_key.pem

#extract and calculate the public key from those private keys to send over the network
openssl pkey -in browser_private_key.pem -pubout -out browser_public.pem
openssl pkey -in server_private_key.pem -pubout -out server_public.pem

#calculating the raw shared secret

##pkeyutl = (public key utility) manually calculate the Elliptic Curve public key directly from a private key
##derive (key derivation) = generating a new cryptographic key from a base secret or from existing keys using a repeatable mathematical function
##inkey = private key
##peerkey = public key received from the other side over internet
##openssl pkeyutl -derive = CPU takes the private key and combines it with the received public key:: a x B = b x A
##*.bin = to keep data in its rawest form (binary 0 1)

openssl pkeyutl -derive -inkey browser_private_key.pem -peerkey server_public.pem -out shared_session_key.bin

#hashing step (HKDF): in TLS 1.3, we run the AES key through a key derivation hashing function-sha256- to ensure uniform randomness to get the final uniform 256-bit AES-GCM session key

##AES = encryption algorithm
##GCM = creating a digital fingerprint to prevent tampering with data by hashing (GHash algorithm) the encrypted block (16 bytes) alongside the unencrypted AAD part (Additional Authentification Data) = TLS Record Header*. It turns block cipher to stream cipher.

##dgst = calculate the cryptographic hash (digest) using a hashing algorithm
##hex = output in hexadecimal

openssl dgst -sha256 -hex shared_secret.bin > session_key.txt

==============================================
*TLS Record Header Metadata:

- Content type (1 byte):: kind of data inside the encrypted payload:
      0x16 for handshake message
      0x17 for Application Data/Web traffic

- Legacy TLS version (2 bytes):: 0x0303: TLS 1.2, 1.3 = initiating encrypted web browsing

- Length (2 bytes):: payload size

